From 560df4a95d61a510193163c7abc8a6f90310864d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:02:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Desktop crash reports, GBA key logging on both sides of
 netplay, old GBA default keys migrated to WASD

- Common/CrashReport: a last-chance handler on Windows (unhandled-exception
  filter, RtlVirtualUnwind walk) and macOS/Linux (fatal-signal handlers on
  an alternate stack, backtrace + dladdr) that writes crash_<stamp>.txt next
  to the session logs with every frame as module+offset, then hands the
  crash back to the OS. Installed from DolphinQt main; stubbed on Android
  (tombstones). MemTools chains its previous handler with the original
  siginfo and grows its alternate stack to 64 KiB so the report fits.
- gba_detect log: 'keys-local' lines (what this machine's own keyboard or
  controller produced for its GBA, plus whether the input gate was open)
  and 'keys' lines (what the emulated GBA received after netplay), one per
  change, 30 per second per socket, overflow counted.
- Launcher: a GBA slot still holding the old T/G/F/H + Q/W defaults gets
  those six keys moved to W/S/A/D + Q/E once; anything else is untouched.
- VS: linker map next to the PDB for offline symbolization.
